0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 508 Td (This study investigates the extent of data-driven instructional supervision) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 494 Td (practices and the level of digital readiness among public secondary school heads in) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 480 Td (the Division of Manila during Academic Year 2025-2026. Employing a) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 466 Td (descriptive-correlational research design, the study surveyed 32 public secondary) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 452 Td (school principals, 128 department heads, and 340 master teachers across six) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 438 Td (congressional districts in Manila.) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 420 Td (Findings indicate that school heads demonstrate a high level of commitment to) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 406 Td (classroom observation analytics \(M = 4.32, SD = 0.48\) and learning outcome) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 392 Td (monitoring \(M = 4.26, SD = 0.51\), while digital infrastructure integration and) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 378 Td (predictive learner intervention scored moderately high \(M = 3.84, SD = 0.62\).) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 364 Td (Pearson product-moment correlation analysis revealed a significant positive) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 350 Td (relationship \(r = 0.76, p < 0.001\) between digital readiness and supervisory) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 336 Td (effectiveness.) Tj ET
0.478 0.075 0.082 rg
