BT /F2 11 Tf 42 654 Td (1.2 Statement of the Problem) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 638 Td (This study aimed to determine the relationship between data-driven instructional) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 624 Td (supervision and digital readiness of public secondary school heads in the Division) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 610 Td (of Manila during AY 2025-2026. Specifically, it sought answers to the following) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 42 596 Td (research questions:) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 578 Td (1. What is the demographic and professional profile of the respondent school heads) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 564 Td (in terms of administrative experience, highest educational attainment, and) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 550 Td (supervisory training hours?) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 532 Td (2. To what extent do public secondary school heads practice data-driven) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 518 Td (instructional supervision across: \(a\) Classroom Observation & Instructional) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 504 Td (Diagnostics, \(b\) Curriculum Alignment & Assessment Analytics, \(c\) Collaborative) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 490 Td (Coaching & Feedback, and \(d\) Professional Learning Community \(PLC\) Facilitation?) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 472 Td (3. What is the level of digital readiness of the respondents in terms of) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 458 Td (technological competence, digital governance, and data literacy?) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 440 Td (4. Is there a significant relationship between the extent of data-driven) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 426 Td (instructional supervision and the level of digital readiness of public secondary) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 412 Td (school heads?) Tj ET
0.12 0.14 0.18 rg
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 394 Td (5. Based on the findings of the study, what Digital Instructional Supervision Action) Tj ET
BT /F3 10 Tf 56 380 Td (Plan may be proposed?) Tj ET
0.478 0.075 0.082 rg
